          },
          "code": "GET_EMPLOYEE_INFO",
          "id": "1768510518970",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768510518971_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a deterministic entity disambiguation agent. Your inputs are a JSON list of people (`person_list_json`), a `person_name`, a `person_number`.\n\nYour goal is to output a single JSON object indicating if `person_name` and/or `person_number` match any DisplayName and/or PersonNumber in `person_list_json`.\n\n### INPUT DATA\n1. Person List - person_list_json: {{$context.$nodes.GET_WORKER_DETAIL.$output.items}} \n2. Person Name - person_name: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_DATA_FROM_USER_INPUT.$output.personName}}\n3. Person Number - person_number: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_DATA_FROM_USER_INPUT.$output.personNumber}}\n\n### ALGORITHM\nIf `person_number` is provided, use MATCHING RULES to match `person_number` with PersonNumber in `person_list_json`.  Else, use MATCHING RULES to match `person_name` with DisplayName in `person_list_json` by following these steps strictly in order:\n\n1. **One person in initial list (count of `person_list_json` is 1):** \n   - If a match is found, set `matchFoundFlag` to `true`.  \n   - If no match is found, set `matchFoundFlag` to `false`.  If `person_number` is not null, set `message` to \"I couldn’t find an employee with person number [person_number].\", else et `message` to \"I couldn’t find an employee with name [person_name].\"\n   - Skip the rest of the steps.\n\n2. **Initial Filtering:** \n   - Filter all candidates in `person_list_json` with PersonNumber matches `person_number` and/or DisplayName matches 'person_name'.\n\n3. **Determine Match Status:**\n   - **One Match Found:** If exactly one person remains after the initial filtering in Step 2, set `matchFoundFlag` to `true`.\n   - **No Match/Ambiguity:** If 0 matches found, or if >1 plausible candidates exist, set `matchFoundFlag` to `false`.\n\n4. **Construct Clarification (Only if matchFoundFlag is false):**\n   - Create a conversational question followed by a bulleted list of ALL candidates in `person_list_json`.\n   - If 0 matches found in Step 3, **Start the `message` with:** \"I couldn’t find an employee named exactly [person_name]\".   If `person_list_json` has entries, also add \"Here are the close matches I found: \\n\\n\" to `message`.  \n   - If >1 plausible candidates exist in Step 3, **Start the `message` with:** \"I found several employees match the name [person_name].  Which [person_name] can I help you with?\".    If `person_list_json` has entries, also add \"Here are the matches I found: \\n\\n\" to `message`. \n   - **Format:** \"- DisplayName - BusinessTitle\"\n   - **Duplicate Name Handling:** If multiple entries in `person_list_json` share the exact same DisplayName, you must append Person Number as distinguisher to *those specific entries* with *Format:* \"- DisplayName - BusinessTitle (Person Number [PersonNumber])\"\n\n### MATCHING RULES\n1. Ignore case differences\n2. Ignore extra spaces\n3. If person_number is provided and not empty:\n   - Match ONLY against PersonNumber using exact normalized equality.\n   - Ignore person_name.\n4. If person_number is empty:\n   - First try exact full-name match:\n     - Compare normalized person_name to normalized DisplayName.\n     - If exactly one employee matches, return it immediately.\n     - Do not consider any other candidates.\n\n   - If no exact full-name match exists:\n     - If person_name has exactly 1 token, allow match against first name or last name.\n     - If person_name has 2 or more tokens, do not use token-only matching.\n     - Do not use fuzzy matching or substring matching\n\n### OUTPUT SCHEMA\nReturn ONLY a raw JSON object. Do not use Markdown code blocks.\n\n{\n  \"matchFoundFlag\": boolean,\n  \"employeePersonId\":  \"number (PersonId of the match) OR null\",\n  \"employeeAssignmentId\": \"number (AssignmentId of the match) OR null\",\n  \"employeeDisplayName\": \"string (DisplayName of the match) OR null\",\n  \"message\": \"String (The clarification text) OR null\"\n}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1768510518970_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"employeePersonId\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"employeeAssignmentId\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"employeeDisplayName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"matchFoundFlag\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"message\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
