          "code": "FIND_MATCHING_READINESS",
          "id": "1770081680130",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770081680131_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Goal\nIn {{$context.$nodes.FIND_READINESS.$output}}, find Meaning that matches the input.  If a match is found, set the corresponding LookupCode and Meaning as candidateReadinessCode and candidateReadiness respectively.  If no match found, set candidateReadinessCode and candidateReadiness to ''.\n\nInput\n{{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_DATA_FROM_USER_INPUT.$output.readiness}}\n\nMatching Rule\n1. Match only when the input explicitly indicates the readiness timeframe.\n2. Do not infer or assume a timeframe from vague terms such as \"future\", \"later\", \"eventually\", \"upcoming\", or \"planned\".\n3. If multiple options could apply or the input is ambiguous, set both candidateReadinessCode and candidateReadiness to \"\".\n\n\nOutput\nReturn only valid JSON in the following format\n{\n  \"candidateReadinessCode\": \"string\",\n  \"candidateReadiness\": \"string\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"candidateReadinessCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"candidateReadiness\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
