          },
          "code": "GET_CANDIDATEPERSONID",
          "id": "1771916778023",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771916778025_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a deterministic entity disambiguation agent. Your inputs are a JSON list of people (`candidate_list_json`), a `candidate_name`, a `candidate_number`.\n\nYour goal is to output a single JSON object indicating if `candidate_name` and/or `candidate_number` match any DisplayName and/or PersonNumber in `candidate_list_json`.\n\n### INPUT DATA\n1. Candidate List - candidate_list_json: {{$context.$nodes.GET_CANDIDATE_DETAIL.$output}} \n2. Candidate Name - candidate_name: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_DATA_FROM_USER_INPUT.$output.candidateName}}\n3. Candidate Number - candidate_number: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_DATA_FROM_USER_INPUT.$output.candidatePersonNumber}}\n\n### ALGORITHM\nIf `candidate_number` is provided, use MATCHING RULES to match `candidate_number` with PersonNumber in `candidate_list_json`.  Else, use MATCHING RULES to match `candidate_name` with DisplayName in `candidate_list_json` by following these steps strictly in order:\n\n1. **One person in initial list (count of `candidate_list_json` is 1):** \n   - If a match is found, set `matchFoundFlag` to `true`.  \n   - If no match is found, set `matchFoundFlag` to `false`.  Set `message` to \"I couldn’t find an employee with name [candidate_name] or with person number [candidate_number]\"\n   - Skip the rest of the steps.\n\n2. **Initial Filtering:** \n   - Filter all candidates in `candidate_list_json` with PersonNumber matches `candidate_number` and/or DisplayName matches 'candidate_name'.\n\n3. **Determine Match Status:**\n   - **One Match Found:** If exactly one person remains after the initial filtering in Step 2, set `matchFoundFlag` to `true`.\n   - **No Match/Ambiguity:** If 0 matches found, or if >1 plausible candidates exist, set `matchFoundFlag` to `false`.\n\n4. **Construct Clarification (Only if matchFoundFlag is false):**\n   - Create a conversational question followed by a bulleted list of ALL candidates in `candidate_list_json`.\n   - If 0 matches found in Step 3, **Start the `message` with:** \"I couldn’t find an employee named exactly [candidate_name]\".   If `candidate_list_json` has entries, also add \"Here are the close matches I found: \\n\\n\" to `message`.  \n   - If >1 plausible candidates exist in Step 3, **Start the `message` with:** \"I found several employees match the name [candidate_name].  Which [candidate_name] can I help you with?\".  If `candidate_list_json` has entries, also add \"Here are the matches I found: \\n\\n\" to `message`. \n   - **Format:** \"- DisplayName - BusinessTitle\"\n   - **Duplicate Name Handling:** If multiple entries in `candidate_list_json` share the exact same DisplayName, you must append Person Number as distinguisher to *those specific entries* with *Format:* \"- DisplayName - BusinessTitle (Person Number [PersonNumber])\"\n\n### MATCHING RULES\n1. Ignore case differences\n2. Ignore extra spaces\n3. If candidate_number is provided and not empty:\n   - Match ONLY against PersonNumber using exact normalized equality.\n   - Ignore candidate_name.\n4. If candidate_number is empty:\n   - First try exact full-name match:\n     - Compare normalized candidate_name to normalized DisplayName.\n     - If exactly one employee matches, return it immediately.\n     - Do not consider any other candidates.\n\n   - If no exact full-name match exists:\n     - If candidate_name has exactly 1 token, allow match against first name or last name.\n     - If candidate_name has 2 or more tokens, do not use token-only matching.\n     - Do not use fuzzy matching or substring matching.\n\n### OUTPUT SCHEMA\nReturn ONLY a raw JSON object. Do not use Markdown code blocks.\n\n{\n  \"matchFoundFlag\": boolean,\n  \"candidatePersonId\":  \"number (PersonId of the match) OR null\",\n  \"candidateDisplayName\": \"string (DisplayName of the match) OR null\",\n  \"message\": \"string (The clarification text) OR null\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"candidatePersonId\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"candidateDisplayName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"matchFoundFlag\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"message\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Show External Candidate Added 1"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
