        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Show Position Type Plan Created"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5022.5,
            "y": 17470
          },
          "code": "SHOW_POSITION_TYPE_PLAN_CREATED",
          "id": "1770426893598",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770426893600_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Role\nYou are the response composer. Your job is to craft a clear, professional, human-friendly answer to the user's current question using ONLY the retrieved data provided below.  Mention that a position type plan is created along with plan name, plan type, position name, business unit name being {{$context.$nodes.GET_POSITION_INFO.$output.items[0].BusinessUnitName}}, department name being {{$context.$nodes.GET_POSITION_INFO.$output.items[0].DepartmentName}}, plan access type and owner name being {{$context.$variables.loggedInPersonDisplayName}}.\n\n## Current Question\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n## Retrieved Data\nNewly created Position type succession plan: {{$context.$nodes.CREATE_POSITION_TYPE_SUCCESSION_PLAN.$output}}\n{{$context.$nodes.REVIEW_PLAN_DETAIL_DEEP_LINK_2.$output}} \n\n## Conversation History (reference only)\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n### Formatting\n- Lead with a direct answer. No preambles like \"Based on the data retrieved...\" or \"I am able to answer.\"\n- When a succession plan is mentioned, at a minimum, show plan name, plan type, job or incumbent or position based on plan type.\n- If candidate type is external, show 'External Candidate' as its Job.\n- Do not expose internal identifiers such as PersonId, AssignmentId, PlanId, context key, etc, except when it's inside a hyperlink.\n- Add a new line before deep link.\n- “When returning deep links, always use a full absolute URL and render it as an HTML anchor with target=\"_blank\" and rel=\"noopener noreferrer\".\n- The hyperlink must open a new tab instead of same tab in browser.\n- Use paragraph blocks or bullet points for clarity."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Show Job Type Plan Created"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7905.59375,
            "y": 17470
          },
          "code": "SHOW_JOB_TYPE_PLAN_CREATED",
          "id": "1770426519320",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770426519323_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Role\nYou are the response composer. Your job is to craft a clear, professional, human-friendly answer to the user's current question using ONLY the retrieved data provided below.  Mention that a new job type plan is created along with plan name, plan type, job name, plan access type and owner name being {{$context.$variables.loggedInPersonDisplayName}}.\n\n## Current Question\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n## Retrieved Data\nNewly created Job type succession plan: {{$context.$nodes.CREATE_JOB_TYPE_SUCCESSION_PLAN.$output}}\n{{$context.$nodes.REVIEW_PLAN_DETAIL_DEEP_LINK_3.$output}} \n\n## Conversation History (reference only)\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n### Formatting\n- Lead with a direct answer. No preambles like \"Based on the data retrieved...\" or \"I am able to answer.\"\n- When a succession plan is mentioned, at a minimum, show plan name, plan type, job or incumbent or position based on plan type.\n- If candidate type is external, show 'External Candidate' as its Job.\n- Do not expose internal identifiers such as PersonId, AssignmentId, PlanId, context key, etc, except when it's inside a hyperlink.\n- Add a new line before deep link.\n- “When returning deep links, always use a full absolute URL and render it as an HTML anchor with target=\"_blank\" and rel=\"noopener noreferrer\".\n- The hyperlink must open a new tab instead of same tab in browser.\n- Use paragraph blocks or bullet points for clarity."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
